Hi,

I would like to run a quick Newhybrids analysis, and the loci subsetting option implemented in dartR seemed to me a simple and reasonable choice.
Everything works fine with testset.gl <http://testset.gl>, but unfortunately when processing my own dataset I've got back the following Error message.

Starting gl.nhybrids
Error in gl.nhybrids(gl = aa.genlight, outfile = "nhyb.txt", outpath = tempdir("g:/Dropbox/2020_Newhybrids"),  :
    Detected Tag Presence/Absence (SilicoDArT) data. Please provide a SNP dataset

I genuinely started with vcfR and adegenet to read and transform vcf. (script as follows)
vcf <- read.vcfR("g:/Dropbox/Newhybrids/2020_XXX.vcf")
aa.genlight <- vcfR2genlight(vcf, n.cores=4)

For me, the two dataset (testset.gl <http://testset.gl> - aa.genlight) seems very similar:
> aa.genlight
 /// GENLIGHT OBJECT /////////

 // 22 genotypes,  10,433 binary SNPs, size: 1011.6 Kb
 5802 (2.53 %) missing data

 // Basic content
   @gen: list of 22 SNPbin

 // Optional content
   @ind.names:  22 individual labels
   @loc.names:  10433 locus labels
   @pop: population of each individual (group size range: 2-8)
   @other: a list containing: elements without names

> testset.gl <http://testset.gl>
 /// GENLIGHT OBJECT /////////

 // 250 genotypes,  255 binary SNPs, size: 752 Kb
 7868 (12.34 %) missing data

 // Basic content
   @gen: list of 250 SNPbin
   @ploidy: ploidy of each individual  (range: 2-2)

 // Optional content
   @ind.names:  250 individual labels
   @loc.names:  255 locus labels
   @loc.all:  255 alleles
   @position: integer storing positions of the SNPs
   @pop: population of each individual (group size range: 1-11)
   @other: a list containing: loc.metrics  latlong  ind.metrics  history  loc.metrics.flags

few lines of the datamatrix:
> as.matrix(aa.genlight)[1:21,1:10]  # see tiny bit of the data
      NW_004569142.1_1209727 NW_004569142.1_1529538 NW_004569142.1_3161537 NW_004569142.1_4074885
SMP15                      0                      0                      0                      0
SMP14                      0                      0                      0                      0
DMP23                      0                      0                      0                      0
DMP24                      0                      0                      0                      0
P01R                       0                      0                      0                      0
26714                      0                      0                      0                      0
26626                      0                      0                      1                      0
26835                      0                      0                      0                      0
3szR                       0                      0                      0                      0
ZH138                      1                      0                      0                      0
ZH106                      0                      1                      0                     NA
ZH136                      0                      0                      0                      0
23974                      2                      2                      1                      1

Also, Is there a simple way to change the dir for the nhyb.txt to save to?

Please excuse me, if these questions are dumb.
And thank you for your kind help in advance!

Hi Lajos,
Have you tried the gl.compliance.check function to see your genlight file is properly formatted?
Cheers,
Olly

—
CSIRO Environomics Future Science Platform
www.csiro.au/environomics <http://www.csiro.au/environomics>

